/-!
# Simple sections in permutation degree eight

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, Theorem 0.1.2(3), condition K, printed pp.4 and
482. The intended calculation classifies every simple quotient of every
subgroup of S₈, and consequently all proper simple sections of an actual
copy of A₈. The target simple group may inhabit any universe.

The base calculation through degree six is proved. The exceptional matrix
models PSL₂(7), PSL₃(2) and SL₃(2), and simple quotients of subgroups
containing Aₙ, are also covered by proved carrier comparisons and normal
subgroup arguments.

The exhaustive intransitive/imprimitive reduction and primitive cases in
degrees seven and eight remain to be supplied. In particular this module
does not yet assert the S₈ section theorem or the A₈ proper-K consequence.
-/
